{"name":"Green Thumb","hex":"#779900","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green thumb","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A natural skill for gardening.","A person with this skill."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green_thumb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Green Thumb (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Green Thumb is a young-adult novel by Rob Thomas, creator of the television series Veronica Mars. It was published in 1999"}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Green_Thumb%28novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Thumb_(novel)"},{"title":"Thumb","blocks":[{"text":"The thumb is the first digit of the hand, next to the index finger. When a person is standing in the medical anatomical position, the thumb is the outermost digit. The Medical Latin English noun for thumb is pollex, and the corresponding adjective for thumb is pollical."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Liam_Thumb.jpg/330px-Liam_Thumb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thumb"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Green_Thumb%28novel%29.jpg/250px-Green_Thumb%28novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Green_Thumb%28novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Green_Thumb%28novel%29.jpg/250px-Green_Thumb%28novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreen_Thumb(novel).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Liam_Thumb.jpg/500px-Liam_Thumb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Liam_Thumb.jpg/1280px-Liam_Thumb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Liam_Thumb.jpg/500px-Liam_Thumb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiam_Thumb.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Sobo_1909_130.png/500px-Sobo_1909_130.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Sobo_1909_130.png/1280px-Sobo_1909_130.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2